#passage(("Can you define what misogyny is? Misogyny has a specific definition in the language: misogyny is the hatred and/or contempt of women. So if I hate women, then I am a misogynistic individual. To say that Islam is \"misogynistic\", for example, then someone has to provide us with a Scripture that explicitly states that \"Islam hates women\", or \"you should hate women\", which does not exist! In fact, Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, said: \"Few things have been made beloved to me of this world..\", and he said that one of them is women. We love women; I have sisters, I have mothers. So this idea of misogyny we don't agree with.", "But we say, explicitly, that men and women are not equal; that is the Islamic position. We say we are different. Our biology is different. So that's what Islam says. Therefore Islam would have certain obligations and commands for women, and would have different obligations and commands for men. For example, if Islam says that a man should grow his beard, we are not going to say to a woman to grow your beard. It doesn't make any sense! Because we are different; that is an example. Certainly, also when it comes to marriage and all of these commands as well, there are different teachings.", "So we believe in gender roles. We believe in marriage a man has a role and a woman has a role. But liberalistic societies do not agree with gender roles. They would say a man can be in a woman's role and a woman can be in a man's role. We say no! A woman has a role and a man has a role, and we say: because God created us in a way, we fit into a specific role; we don't fit into another role. Our psychology is like this. So in Islam, yes, the man would take the decisions in marriage relationship between him and his wife. That does not mean the wife is now a lesser human being. Islam doesn't say that.", "In fact, some people can even argue that what women do is more important that what men do. So the next generation, taking care of the next generation of people, what the future will be, is dependent on the mother that raises the children in the house. The father's presence is very important. We're not making a comparison, but I am saying some people can even make that argument. And that is why you'd see, when certain people try to destroy a community, a society, a civilisation, they always target the Women! They target the women, they target the education system, because this is the future of the civilisation.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Dismantles French Nationalism And Racist Ideologies! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CTdeXBAESWc", ((256, "4:16–5:10"), (310, "5:10–5:52"), (357, "5:57–6:31"), (403, "6:43–7:12"),))
