#passage(("Islam doesn't say talk to men is Haram (prohibited). It's a specific type of man; we should not be generalising it to everyone. So if it's a specific type of man, there must be a reason. What is a non-Mahram in the Islamic perspective? A non-Mahram in the Islamic perspective is someone you can marry. That means that there is sexual tension that can exist between you and the individual. Sexual attraction, all of these things, can exist between you and the individual. So, limiting the contact between these two individuals, because that person has a specific category. But, for example, me speaking to my brother, my father, or my grandfather: these are all men still, and I'm allowed to speak to them. This idea doesn't exist, and even the woman, she can have her hair out when she's speaking to her family members, male or non-male.", "Can you define what is Oppression? Oppression is unjust treatment. So, these are limitations, what you're referring to. But then, you're oppressed by the country you're living in, because there's so many things you cannot do. So all of the Western women are oppressed, because western women cannot drink and drive, for example; they're all oppressed. So, if we use the term oppression there, then you have to say that all Western women are oppressed. Wherever you live, wherever you are, there has to be certain limitations to the things that you can do and the things that you cannot do.", "Now, when it comes to the Islamic rules, depends on the rule that you ask, there is a reason. Being around non-Mahram men: these are two genders that will be attracted to one another. Prophetﷺ said: when you're alone with a woman, the third person is Satan. So Satan tries to beautifies the woman for the man, and also the woman, her heart sways for the man; it's vice versa. It happens with both of them. When you talk about travel: when a woman will become in a place when she's alone, she doesn't have any protection. It's long distances. She'd be tired