erent. It will be optimal for the situation of the man and the situation of the woman. So whatever command that is there for a man, that is not for a woman, it is because it befits her nature as a woman, and it is the best command, or option, or situation, that she can be in. And the same for a man.", "Allahﷻ says to a man (and no one complains about that): Man, you have to go and work, you have to provide for your woman, you have to provide housing and clothing, and everything for her. She doesn't need to participate when it comes to the financial aspects of the relationship; this is your responsibility. You have to protect her if there's any danger; you're responsible for her, you are a shepherd and you'll be responsible for your flock. So if any danger takes place, you are the one responsible, you need to protect her, even if you're going to lose your life in that fight. So these are things that Allahﷻ commands the man, and you don't see the man coming, complaining \"Oh, why did Allah..?\", \"This is oppressive!\". No one says that; we accept: OK, Allahﷻ told me I have to work, my life is going to be more difficult, no one is going to give me Mahr (marital gift: dowry) and then pay my rent and pay my food; no one is going to do that for me. As a man I have to go and work, and because I'm a man, these are the commands that I need to keep up. Therefore, I follow. I know this is what works for me as a man. Allahﷻ knows my nature, Allahﷻ knows the best option for me, and what I should be doing, and why I should be doing it.", "When it comes to physicality: if I bring a 20-year-old woman and a 15-year-old boy and they fight, who's going to win? Generally, in most cases? Why is he going to win? Because he's got a physical nature that is God-given that the woman does not have. He's got muscle mass, more muscle mass, faster reaction speed, tissues, and all of these things. So if they're not the same when it comes to the physicality and power and who can overcome the other, then one can be allowed to go out at night, he is able to protect himself, and one would not.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Lady Questions Muslim About Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wloKwQx2KcA", ((396, "6:36–7:26"), (450, "7:30–8:11"), (499, "8:19–8:56"), (541, "9:01–9:24"), (567, "9:27–9:56"), (600, "10:00–10:33"), (639, "10:39–11:28"), (744, "12:24–12:56"),))
