#passage(("\"Women are more free in Islam than any other religion.\" What do you mean by \"free\"? Yeah, we are going to say women are more free, but our definition of freedom is completely different from your definition of freedom. So, what happens a lot in conversations like this is: terms are not defined. It's buzzwords that people throw out, because they follow propaganda, they never left their basement, they never left their country, and then they're just repeating what they hear from people who are spreading false information about Islam. And they throw these buzzwords, and you have these followers that heard the same buzzwords: \"My favorite streamer said it, therefore it must be true\"!", "Islamic women are more free than anyone: they know the Truth! What is more freedom for someone than to know what the Truth is? Why you exist in this life, and what's going to happen to you in the afterlife? What is more freedom than to be safe and have tranquility that in the afterlife you're going to be safe; if you die as a Muslim, you're going to enter Paradise? There's nothing more freeing than this. There's nothing more freeing than knowing what is your role in this life, how God created you: God created you as a female, and you have a role that will fit you. Not giving you roles of the man and then giving them to the female; that's not going to make you free. That's not what freedom is. Freedom is being modest. Not your guys's definition of freedom: as many clothes as you take off, the more free you are! As someone said, \"then the animals are the most free, because they're wearing nothing\". So, if this is your definition of freedom, then you have a skewed definition of freedom. So, we need to define terms.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Asmongold Responds - Women Are Oppressed In Islam? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sGEADBXUEFo", ((417, "6:57–7:32"), (458, "7:38–8:32"),))

