#passage(("Let me give you the contrast of what Islam teaches about women, not what Christianity teaches. What does Islam teach about women? Islam teaches, like the Prophet told us: النِّساءُ شَقائقُ الرِّجالِ (men and women are generally equal). There's no statement like this in the Bible. The Prophet told us: (the best of you are the best to their wives, and I'm the best to my wife). And that's why I told you, the Prophet was the example for us. He didn't beat his women. He treated them in the most, utmost respect and honour. This is what Islam teaches.", "A woman, in EVERY level, in Islam is taken care of. When you get married to your wife, she doesn't need to lift a finger at work. YOU HAVE TO WORK! You have to provide for the house. You provide clothing. You provide sustenance. YOU DO ALL OF THAT. And if she works, her money is HER money. There is no religion that brought honour to women the way Islam did. Women before Islam, they were just objects, used for fornication and all of that. They were not allowed inheritance; Islam allowed them inheritance. They were not allowed to own property. Islam is the first religion to allow them to own property, when Western countries, they were NOT allowed to own properties.", "So nobody can come and point any finger at the treatment of women in Islam, especially if he's a Christian. Christian or atheist, or any other religion or faith, nobody can come and say anything about the teachings of Islam. So my recommendation to you is to stick to the statement you made. You said \"That's why I don't follow Islam\" or \"I wouldn't follow Islam\". Then stick to the same statement about your Christianity. Then you should say \"I'm not going to be a Christian, because these are the teachings in my book\". Shouldn't that be a consistent position?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Left In Utter Shock After Attempting To Criticise Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cFKbacM6CFs", ((1039, "17:19–17:54"), (1094, "18:14–18:43"), (1129, "18:49–19:19"),))
