#passage(("Let's be people of evidence and let's tackle this rationally. Let's accept this idea that Islam is a religion made to fit the patriarchy. It's made for the desire of the man. It's made to help the men and it is made to praise them. Why would the religion made to suit the desire of the man tell you that the man is prohibited for him to wear gold and silk, but for the women, that they can wear gold and silk? Why would the religion to fit the desire of the man and to oppress the woman give the custody of the children, when the children are young, to the mother? I have multiple stories of men that cry, that come, that complain to me that \"my wife is preventing me from seeing my kids\"; the wife took the kids. They can't even see their kids. Islam gives the custody of the children to the mother and it doesn't give it to the father. So, why would the religion made to suit the desire of the man do that?", "Why would the religion made to suit the desire of the man say that the man is supposed to pay the mahar, a marital gift that can go to hundreds of thousands of dollars in some cases, and not be like the Hindu customs, for example: \"the woman is going to bring you the marital gift. The woman is going to do everything and you just sit down\", like they do in the Hindu culture? Why would the religion that is made to suit the desire of the man putting the woman, the mother, three times before the father?", "Why would the Prophet Muhammad, before his death, he says \"treat women well\"? Before his death, over 100,000 companions there, one of the most important advice he's going to give the people before he passes away, and he says: \"Treat women well.\" Why didn't he say \"Treat your husbands well\", or \"listen to your husband\", or \"obey your husband\"? Why does Islam say: \"If you have two daughters or two sisters, and you look after them, and you're good to them, that they will be a shield for you from the hellfire\"? Why is the religion made to suit the desire of the man honoring the woman in that way? Why did the Prophet say \"The best of you is the best of your wives\"? Why didn't he say \"the best of your husband\"?", "If it's a religion made to suit the desire of the man, why is the religion that is made to suit my desires forcing me to go to war and die and lose my limbs and suffer, so I can protect the woman, and saying to the woman that the woman can stay back, it's okay, you don't have to do any of that? Why isn't it saying: \"Women, you go fight, and the men sit back, relax\"? Why is it telling me I have to provide money and housing after marriage to my wife, and I have to do all of that, and I have to look after my wife financially, if it's a religion made to suit my desire? Why is it not saying the woman is supposed to provide for me? Why is it saying that I'm the guardian of my family, that I'm the protector, and I'm going to be asked upon my flock? I have to look after my family, I have to protect it. If it's a religion made to suit my desire and to suit the desire of men, why is it putting that responsibility upon me? Why is a religion made to suit the desire of the man giving women all of these privileges? Why?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is Islam A Religion Made For The Men?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OzxyEO708yI", ((216, "3:36–4:57"), (297, "4:57–5:32"), (335, "5:35–6:07"), (367, "6:07–7:11"),))
