#passage(("So in Islam, how does Islam view the relationship between men and women? The woman is elevated and respected in every level, either as a Mother, as a Wife or as a Daughter. In The Quran, Allah blames both Adam and Eve from eating from the Tree (Quran7:22). It was a fault of both of them. Both of them were deceived by Satan (Quran7:19-24). This is not the fault of the woman. There's no such thing as the Original Sin. I'm not the one who ate from the Tree, so you cannot say I'm a sinner because of what someone else did in the past! So the woman has no blame in Islam; that's the first. I want to just remove this idea of blame. There's no blame on the woman in Islam. She's a Creation of God, and when it comes to accountability and responsibility towards God, she's equal to a man. But when it comes to what you should do and what you shouldn't do in the dynamics between men and women, it is not like this.", "But first we talk about a woman as a Mother. A man came to The Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, and then he said to The Prophet Muhammad: \"who should I love the most, or be good to the most, after you?\" Prophet Muhammad said \"your mother\". Then the man said \"then who?\". He said \"your mother\". He said \"then who?\". He said \"your mother\". He said \"then who?\". He said \"then your father\"! So the woman is put first. Allah says in The (Quran17:23): Allah commands you to only worship Him AND to be good to your parents. Allah says in The (Quran31:15): even if your parents are not believers, you have to be good to them. Prophet Muhammad, in a tradition, he said that (if you're being good to your mother, it's as if Paradise is under her feet). By you being good to her, it is a path for you to go to paradise. So this is the woman as a mother.", "She takes the children in the beginning, if there's a divorce between a man and a woman in Islam, when they're young, when they mostly need the mother, till they reach an age in which they can tell the difference, and then they can choose who they want to be with. But if a woman were to get married to someone else, then the man takes the child, because now she's with another man. Very logical, very fundamental teachings to do with everything to do in societies. The West is lost because of that! There is no Guidance of what you do in certain situations. But Islam gives you holistic guidance. So the woman as a mother, she's given the right to have the child if there is divorce, when he's young, to take care of him, to breastfeed him and all of that, because the child needs the mother the most at this age.", "Now, what about being wife? Allah says explicitly in The Quran, in chapter:4 verse:19: وَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ (and treat them fairly and goodly in everything). You have to be treating them fairly and goodly. So this is the treatment that you need to treat your wife. In Islam, Allah gives you the responsibility in the relationship as a man. You're the leader in the relationship. You provide for the woman. You take care of the woman and you protect the woman. And in exchange of value, the woman does her role, which is taking care of the children, and being a home for the man, being a peaceful abode for the man. So Islam gives the commands exactly to which who should do what, and when they should do it.", "As a daughter, Prophet Muhammad said: (if you take care of your daughter and you be good to her, she will be a veil for you from The Hellfire) in the Afterlife. So when it comes to women, Islam is fairly and justly treating women on every level, but it also gives them commands.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “What Does The Bible Actually Say About Women? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z8-gsP8mmuk", ((503, "8:23–9:14"), (560, "9:20–9:54"), (600, "10:00–10:35"), (640, "10:40–11:26"), (692, "11:32–11:42"),))
