// U ML098:42-107 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("First of all, the Prophetﷺ ('alayhi salatu wa salam: peace and blessings be upon him) explicitly told us not to hit our wives. The Prophet said: لاَ تَضْرِبُوا إِمَاءَ اللّه (Do not hit the women servants of Allah). So this is clearly a false claim to make about Islam. The verse is talking about a very specific situation, and it gives steps for this specific situation.", "Allah says: (forsake them in bed); meaning sleep with them in the same bed but don't have intercourse with them, as a form of showing disapproval for their actions, for disobedience. And when we say disobedient, meaning they're not given the husband one of his rights. Now, what kind of rights are they? They are things that are good. Prophetﷺ told us: إنَّما الطَّاعةُ في المَعروفِ (Obedience is in that which is good). So she's denying the husband one of his rights. It could be any of the rights of the husbands that Islam legislates as the rights of the husband.", "Then Allah uses the word اِضْرِبُوهُنَّ. Now the word اِضْرِبُوهُنَّ here doesn't mean \"beat\", because \"beat\" in the English language is a clear false translation. You can use \"discipline\", you can use any term you want to use, but to use specifically \"beat\" is false, because \"beat\" in the English language means severe hitting, and that is explicitly prohibited in the Hadith (Prophetic sayings). Prophetﷺ told us that this ضَرْبْ, whatever this word means, is غَيْرَ مُبَرِّحْ. What does غَيْرَ مُبَرِّحْ mean? It means it's not severe. This type of discipline that's supposed to take place is not severe. Prophetﷺ said: (you cannot hit the face). You cannot hit severely where you leave a mark, or you break a bone, or do any of these things. So it's NOT beating. If I kill a fly or something, or do like this and kill a fly, nobody's going to say you beat the fly. It's not the right term to use in this case, so beating is completely false. I use the term \"discipline\" because I don't think there's a proper word in the English language that you can use.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| 5 Reasons I Left Islam?! Hijabi Says Christians Will Go To Heaven?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wIhGWmIQTJY", ((156, "2:36–2:50"), (196, "3:16–4:01"), (255, "4:15–5:07"),))
