// U ML335:267-379 | The Muslim Lantern | 7
#passage(("In chapter 4 of the Quran, verse 34, the verse is: الرِّجَالُ قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ وَبِمَا أَنفَقُوا مِنْ أَمْوَالِهِمْ ۚ So Allah's established something which is called قوامة (Qawamah), i.e. the man has a leadership in the relationship, in the family structure, traditional family structure of a man and a woman. There has to be someone in charge, either the man or the woman. Islam puts the one in charge for the man for two reasons. It says: بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ (what Allah gave them over women): for example the physical strength, their protective nature, the fact that they do not go through menstruation, which can affect the judgement or emotions. All of these types of things. You can open any Tafsir (exegesis) which will talk about that. So that's the first reason.", "The second reason is: بِمَا أَنفَقُوا مِنْ أَمْوَالِهِمْ (with the money that they are providing for that woman). Because in an Islamic relationship the man is the one who provides. He pays the Mahr (Dowry), he provides the housing, he provides everything from a financial point of view. So because he's got this responsibility; naturally when you got responsibility it equals authority. Because if you have responsibility with no authority, that's what slavery is. You put responsibility on a slave and he's got no authority, that's what slavery is. So whenever there is responsibility there has to be authority equal to that responsibility.", "So that's the beginning of the verse. Then Allahﷻ says (Quran 4:34): فَالصَّالِحَاتُ قَانِتَاتٌ حَافِظَاتٌ لِّلْغَيْبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ اللَّهُ ۚ So Allah says (the righteous women, they are قانتات): they pray in the night, they're close to their Creator, to The Lord, they obey Allahﷻ. And حافظات: they preserve their private parts; they don't cheat behind their husbands. So Allah for us gave the example of a righteous woman.", "Then now we go into a disobedient woman (Quran4:34): وَاللَّاتِي تَخَافُونَ نُشُوزَهُنَّ (But those wives from whom you fear recalcitrance). So here now we've got steps for a specific type of woman. First, this verse in The Quran is not saying about all wives. It's talking about a woman that starts problems and becomes disobedient in things which are the rights of the husband. So in Islam there's rights; things which are the rights of the husband. So the woman has certain rights she needs to fulfil to the husband, and her husband has certain rights he needs to fulfil to the wife. So both of them can become ناشز. Both of them can become disobedient from that sense. Allah also in The Quran, in the same Surah, he speaks about the man: if he does نشوز, what does the woman does? So it's not only the woman. A man can leave his rights and a woman can leave her rights.", "So Allah says then: this disobedient, how do you deal with her? What does Allah say in the first thing? He says: فَعِظُوهُنَّ. What does عظوهنّ mean? (give them advice), speak to them nicely, advise them nicely. And Allah says ف, and الفاء here is for ترتيب (Order). So these things have to be done in order. You cannot jump to step three before step two and you cannot jump to step two before step one. The Quran is in Arabic language and you should know a little bit of Arabic; you should know there's something called ترتيب (order), and these أحرف (Letters) in Arabic language have functions.", "So the first thing is فَعِظُوهُنَّ: does Allah say any time period? Does Allah say فعظوهن أسبوعا؟ (Advise them for a week?), فعظوهن شهرا؟ (Advise them for a month?) No! Allah says فَعِظُوهُنَّ and he leaves it open, which means you will give advice until you're sure that the advice is not working anymore; then you can move into the next step. Now everyone knows his wife; you know when what you're saying, she doesn't care anymore about what you are saying. Then you move to the step two: وَاهْجُرُوهُنَّ فِي الْمَضَاجِعِ (then if they persist, forsake them in bed). وَاهْجُرُوهُنَّ فِي الْمَضَاجِعِ means that both of you will sleep in the same bed, but you're not going to have intercourse with her. Do a هجر of her (forsake her) from a sexual standpoint; you're not going to have intercourse with that woman. And that can be very psychologically impactful on a woman, because the woman then she feels she's not beautiful, she's not desired. He is literally next to her, but he's not even engaging with her. So it's a form of punishment as well.", "And then the last thing it says: وَاضْرِبُوهُنَّ (and finally, strike them). And then Allah says: فَإِنْ أَطَعْنَكُمْ فَلَا تَبْغُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيلًا ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيرًا (But if they obey you once more, seek no means against them. Indeed, Allah is ever Exalted and Grand.) Allah finishes the verse very strongly there. Allah says: إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيرًا (Allah is above and Almighty), which means: do not think that you do something to that woman if she now obeys and she stops being disobedient. You have to remember that Allah is above you, and Allah is stronger than you; then you stop as Allah commanded you to stop, if she stops being disobedient.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tunisian Girl Questions Muslim On Women's Rights! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l68vK6nDhbA", ((831, "13:51–14:36"), (879, "14:39–15:07"), (907, "15:07–15:27"), (931, "15:31–16:02"), (966, "16:06–16:31"), (995, "16:35–17:24"), (1049, "17:29–17:57"),))
