// U ML361:103-250 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("And the women that you fear disobedience from them: disobedience here is in context to the teachings of the Quran and Sunnah, meaning the rights of the husband. So the husband has certain rights. So, not general disobedience, but specific disobedience in the rights that he has over her. For example, the husband has a right over the woman, that she has intercourse with him. If she stops having intercourse with him, denies him intercourse, for example, then she's being disobedient. Because he's your husband, and where is he going to go if you're not going to give him intercourse? So, that's a right that Islam gives. So, if she doesn't give him that right, for example, then she's a disobedient woman. It's called the ناشز.", "The second step is: you move away from them in the bed, meaning you both sleeping on the same bed. Because some people misunderstand that they go sleep on the couch. No, you're both sleeping in the same bed, but you're not having intercourse with her, because that breaks the woman from within, because her only weapon against the man, or main weapon, is intercourse.", "Then the last step here: the word ضرب here, which can mean hit, it can mean physical contact between two things. And I don't want to say hit because I don't like the English language explanation. This physical contact can have different levels. I'll give an example. The prophet said, there's an action that we do when we don't find water, because we do ablution before we pray. But sometimes there is no water. So there is an action that we do. It's called تيمّم. The prophet says, do ضرب, the same word, on the floor. You know how we do ضرب? Like this. And then we do our hands like this on the floor. So does that sound like hitting and beating? No! So the word does not necessitate what people understand of it. That's why the word hit in English does not really translate correctly from that word.", "So let's take physical contact as a word. Then that physical contact, what level can it go to? The prophet and the companions, they explained to us. You can do more, but there is the limit. The limit is: you don't leave a mark and this and that. There is, sometimes, there is discipline needed. Sometimes, the wife does not view you as a man anymore. So, sometimes, you have to assert dominance in a specific way. We're not saying be abusive. We're not saying be aggressive. We're not saying hit your wife and leave marks. We're not saying any of that. We're saying a certain level of assertiveness. If I hold my wife, for example, like this, and I sit her down, for example, then she knows, this is a serious thing now. Or I give her a little press on the shoulder. Any husband and wife do that anyways. This is a general thing. This is what the verse is referring to.", "And then we look at the life of the Prophet. The last thing: it is recommended that you don't hit at all. Based on what? Based on the Prophet, because he's an example for us, as the Quran says. And Aisha said the Prophet عليه الصلاة والسلام (Peace and blessings be upon him), he never hit any of his wives. So if you're a Muslim, you want to be the best Muslim? Then you don't do hitting at all. Even though it is permissible in the way I told you, if you want to be the best Muslim, the best behaviour according to Islam is that you don't hit at all. No hitting at all, and that's what Imam Shafi'i said as well. He said the best of men, they would not hit, because the Prophet عليه الصلاة والسلام said the best of you are the best to their wives and the best to their families.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Mexican Catholic Asks Difficult Questions To Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xSJWDDYfD_Y", ((300, "5:00–5:37"), (375, "6:15–6:34"), (406, "6:46–7:52"), (474, "7:54–9:22"), (565, "9:25–10:04"),))
