#passage(("We know from the sayings of the prophet, peace be upon him, the actions of the prophet, peace be upon him, that it's not beating, like beat them senseless etc.; it's more symbolic than anything. Because we have to look at it from the angle of before the Quran was revealed: a man in Arabia especially, he could beat his wife left, right and center, however much he wished, and the Quran limited it down to [ghayr mubarrih], which is basically not hitting at all. So it basically stopped people from abusing their wives, and that's the context of the Quran in light of what the prophet, peace be upon him, and the companion said.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood's Top Ten Arguments Debunked!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YPvZ_xNePzo", ((606, "10:06–10:48"),))
