#passage(("In many cases, women will inherit more than men. All you have to do really is just to open and read the Quran, rather than what many people do: hear Islamophobic lying and then think that the Quran actually says what they hear. The verse itself mentions different distributions in different cases. For instance, the same verse of the Quran in Chapter:4 mentions that if someone dies and then there's only one daughter left, the daughter takes half of the inheritance (anNisa4:11). In some situations, men will take more than women, in which case the man takes two (anNisa4:176): if someone dies and he has children, boys and girls. Why? Because the financial responsibility of a woman in Islam is not the same as the financial responsibility of a man.", "Now, if my daughter wants to get married, all that happens is a man comes, he offers her a dowry, which is a marital gift, and he marries her. She has no financial burden from an Islamic point of view. After marriage, the man has the responsibility of taking care of her. So he'll provide for her the place of living, the sustenance, the food, the clothing, all of these things. So she has no financial burden from that aspect. If the girl is before marriage, then I'm the father, I'm supposed to provide for her. So the woman, in every case and scenario, she's provided for by someone. If she becomes a mother and the husband dies, the son provides for the mother. So in every case, the woman is provided for.", "Now, in the case of a man: there is a lot more financial responsibility. You are the one who's going to take care of the woman. You're going to spend on yourself and her. When you're getting married, you are the one who's going to bring the marital gift, the dowry. You are the one who's going to be working and need to have a financial burden to take care of your family and/or your sister. So because the financial responsibilities are not the same, the man would take more than the woman would take in that case of inheritance. But that's only one scenario, for example, or a few scenarios, in which the man will have more financial burden and responsibility than the woman. So it is not the case, as you claimed, that the men take two times the women in inheritance. That's simply false.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Confronts Muslim On Women Treatment But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B7p5zJqM40w", ((253, "4:13–5:58"), (432, "7:12–7:49"), (471, "7:51–8:35"),))
