#passage(("\"A woman is worth half a man\" is very different from saying \"a testimony of a woman is worth half a man\". They're absolutely not the same thing.", "The testimony of men and women in Islam: in certain aspects, in certain teachings, in certain commands, the testimony of one man will be equal to the testimony of two women. For instance, like this case, where this verse is called آية الدَّيْن (the Verse of Debt). So if there is a debt written and you need witnesses that you've taken debt from someone, etc. So this is the issues of dealings and loaning and buying and selling, these issues, and these types of dealings. Generally, because they have expertise in these fields and they deal with these fields more than women would deal with these fields, a testimony of a man can be equal to two in a situation like this. Similarly, in a situation of حدود (Hudood), let's say punitive laws and punishments, where emotions can get involved and can influence a woman's memory, essentially how things happened, etc., or her judgement, generally, of her testimony: in this case, also, a testimony of a man can be equal to two women.", "But in other cases, scenarios and situations, a testimony of a woman can be taken over a testimony of a man. In certain cases, a testimony of one woman will be taken over a testimony of one man. We have a narration of the Prophetﷺ where there was a black slave woman, and her testimony was taken over a Companion's testimony, someone who was a Companion to Prophet Muhammad. He was an Arab. He was a free man. He was a Companion. Her testimony was taken over his testimony. Why? Because the issue was to do with pregnancy and children and giving birth. The issues where men are more familiar, you have a testimony of one man equal to two women. In issues where women are more familiar, the testimony can even be taken over the testimony of a man. So it just depends on the situation, and it is not like a rule that is applied in every case and scenario and situation.", "But in the case of debt, where the verse is specifically talking about that, yes, testimony is taken. And the verse mentions the reason: أَن تَضِلَّ إِحْدَاهُمَا فَتُذَكِّرَ إِحْدَاهُمَا ٱلْأُخْرَىٰ (That maybe one of them would forget). These issues are not issues which they would usually deal with normally, loaning and buying and selling. (So if one woman forgets, the other one would remind her) (alBaqara2:282).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Confronts Muslim On Women Treatment But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B7p5zJqM40w", ((78, "1:18–1:21"), (101, "1:41–2:34"), (157, "2:37–3:29"), (215, "3:35–3:55"),))
