#passage(("The Prophet was asked what is a deficiency. He said the deficiency is in testimony. \"Deficiency\" is not the right word, by the way. He said the \"reduction\", which is the right word I would use, because it means نَقْص, to reduce from something, like Allah says in the Quran نَنقُصُهَا about the Ard (Earth) (arRa'd13:41): نَنقُصُهَا مِنْ أَطْرَافِهَا (we reduce it from its parts), so \"reduction\". So, he says reduction in testimony, that is the reduction in the mind, the testimony, and the other reduction in the religion, which is that when she goes into menstruation, she doesn't have to pray and do religious obligations.", "So the Hadith already responds to these things. The Prophet already explained it. He's not saying that they're less intelligent or that they're more sinners than men or less righteous servants, or whatever. No! He said this is what we mean. When the Prophet says a reduction in something, he's referring to a reduction in responsibility, actually. Even in the testimony: testimony is a responsibility. Why? Because false testimony means you will be lashed! So if you require 4 people to testify, and 3 say something and 1 doesn't, they will ALL be lashed. False testimony in Islam is not a joke. You cannot simply come and testify to something. So this is a reduction in responsibility. It's not a reduction in a way which insults women, in any way for sure.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Romanian Christian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RCeSQlWHPxI", ((1333, "22:13–22:48"), (1371, "22:51–23:58"),))
