#passage(("That narration came in a context of the Persians, specifically having a woman as the ruler of their nation. Now, there are some scholars who would say this narration refers to that specific event in which, as the Prophet said, the nation did not succeed; that woman was not successful for that nation. But how do we understand the Hadith is a question. We understand the Hadith that there are exceptions to this rule. But generally, that's not who you would put as a leader. So the leader of the Muslim is a man. When we say the leader, we're talking about the highest leader of the Muslims: the Imam al Mu'minin (Leader of the Believers) has to be a man, and cannot be a woman.", "There are exceptions. Yes, even the Quran mentions one. The Quran mentions Bilqees, for example, the Quran mentions at the time of Solomon (anNaml27:15-44). And Allah praises her as a ruler. He praises her intelligence. He praises her as a ruler. And she was a woman. So you can have exceptions to the case. But still, did she just succeed without the help of any men? No, that was not the case. She had advisors that are men. She had men fighting in her armies. This is another way to look at the narration from scholars' reviews: absolute success will never come by a woman being the leader.", "Now, when we talk about leadership, anyways, what are the qualities that are necessary in a leader? Men in general are not going to be subdued by a female. That's how their nature is. They are not going to be submissive and subdued by a woman. That is the case when it comes to most men, generally. Of course, I'm not talking about some freaks in the West. These are not the general population of men. I'm talking about actual, REAL MEN, men who go to jobs, work 9 to 5, and go to construction and build societies. They're not going to accept a woman as their leader. That is normally and generally the case. They will need someone, a man like them, to subdue them, to make them submissive to him when it comes to leadership.", "Also, a woman, naturally, goes through a menstrual period. Her psychology and her emotions, how she is as a being, is completely different from a man. A man doesn't go through a monthly cycle. It does not affect his hormones and decision-making and his reliance on emotions, as it does with a woman. That can be a huge influence when someone is a leader. You need to be, at all times, in the right mind and state when you're ruling a people or individuals. You cannot have something like that influencing your decisions. We would take the narration the way it is, because Islamically, that's the Islamic position, a woman can't be the leader of the whole Nation. That's not something that is allowed.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Gets Questioned On The Treatment Of Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jtI_KJQc9SM", ((308, "5:08–5:44"), (351, "5:51–6:22"), (385, "6:25–7:18"), (440, "7:20–8:03"),))
