#passage(("Of course, Iran is not a perfect example anyways to give. But women are not allowed to work, women are not allowed to study, women are not allowed to go out of the house, essentially, in Iran, according to this guy. Let's again talk about the FACTS. So let's first look at this article by Forbes. What is Forbes telling us about Iran? The article is titled the following: \"Set to take over tech: 70% of Iran's science and engineering students are women\". Then we have this other article by Quartz: \"The West is way behind Iran and Saudi Arabia when it comes to women in science\". What does it tell us? It tells us: \"In Iran, nearly 70% of graduates in science, technology, engineering and mathematics are women,\" \"a higher percentage than any other country\". And then it says: \"Nearby Oman, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE are close, each boasting over 60% female graduates in science\", \"still more than the rest of the world\"!", "Anybody can check videos online of women in Tehran clearly walking with their hair out. Go to Egypt, Morocco, Tunisia, Syria, Lebanon.", "You got to define terms. What do you mean by freedom? Freedom is a general term. If he meant by freedom that they're not allowed to study or work, he's been refuted clearly! You've got to define what you mean by these terms.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Asmongold Responds - Women Are Oppressed In Islam? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sGEADBXUEFo", ((898, "14:58–16:15"), (987, "16:27–16:34"), (1006, "16:46–17:00"),))
