#passage(("What do you mean, go around women as you feel like? There's no such thing in the Quran. The Quran limits the opposite gender interaction more than any other faith out there. In Islam, you're not allowed to touch women.", "For example, the Bible, the New Testament would teach that a woman should not assume authority over a man (1Timothy2:12), and what Paul would teach (1Corinthians14:34): a woman should not teach a man and should remain silent in the church. Paul said that women shouldn't teach men. From a logical sense, this teaching is completely irrational, and that proves that this teaching is not from God. When you read (2Timothy3:16), for example, it says \"all scripture is eternal and useful for teaching and rebuking for all times\". That's what the Bible says. (Psalms119:160) will say the same thing. And I could quote different scriptures to demonstrate that what the Bible teaches is that the scriptures of its own is eternal and it is for all times.", "In Islam, a woman can teach someone, or can say something. The wives of the Prophetﷺ, after his death, they taught the Companions, they taught people, they taught them knowledge that they didn't know. We don't have an issue with that, but there's boundaries. For example, a man cannot touch a woman of the opposite gender. There's no physical interaction between a man and a woman of the opposite gender in Islam, which you're not gonna find in Christianity: they shake hands and do whatever they like, and hug and kiss and everything. There's no intercourse before marriage. There is no adultery in Islam. There is no being alone with a woman that is not closely related to you, or your wife, or your family member. You cannot be alone in one place with her. That's also prohibited in Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Catholic Grandfather Examines The Teachings Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tyYeayKMNwM", ((1596, "26:36–27:10"), (1697, "28:17–29:58"), (1804, "30:04–30:40"),))

