#passage(("By the way, that statement is not true. Which studies that you have that shows that in the Middle East it's higher than anywhere else in the world? Africa is not necessarily a Muslim country, as you know. This study, we need to look at it. How many people did they conduct? I brought you a study in the UN, which I believe nearly 100,000 women. This is the biggest study done by the UN, United Nations. I'm not talking about some random study where someone surveyed 10 women and they came to a conclusion that fits their narrative. So if you present something, you need evidences for it.", "But there is a projection of this idea, of course, in the West, because the West wants to convince themselves that the people in Africa and the people in the Muslim countries are a bunch of barbarics that need to be educated and enlightened, and they are the \"white saviour\" that is going to come and do that! They have this narrative that they want to come to us with. But in reality, when you look at true studies, that's not true in any way, shape, or form. People can do the research on that.", "But again, even if there were cases of abuse, it's definitely not one of the highest, but if there's cases of abuse, that cannot be correlated to the religious texts, because there are good and bad people everywhere. There's 2 billion Muslims in the world. Quarter of the population of the planet, you can say, if not a third very soon, of the population of the planet are Muslims. So when you have some people somewhere doing something wrong, obviously that's going to be the case. Now the Prophet explicitly in one narration said: (do not hit the woman-servants of Allah). So he prohibited that. The Prophet explicitly prohibited any hitting the face, any breaking bones or any severe hitting of a woman. The Prophetﷺ, his wife said \"the Prophet never hit any woman\". And he's the example for us that the Quran tells us to follow (alAhzab33:21). So if the religion teaches us that, and some random idiot goes and does something wrong, of course, there's no correlation there between the religion and an action of a group of bad apples somewhere.", "That's an article. So that's not a scientific study. Who conducted the study? Who did the survey? How many people were surveyed? I can write you an article today and I'll tell you that 100% of Western women get abused. That doesn't mean anything. Which organisation went there and surveyed the women? And what were the questions asked? What was the number of people? All of these things are available on the UN website, for example, for the study I gave you.", "My problem is that a lot of people are not familiar with primary sources, are not familiar with proper researching. And a lot of people have a confirmation bias. They would accept information that is in line with their bias. They're biased already. They're grown up watching media and hearing all the news. Their bias already believes this is true. So if something says what I believe, of course I like it! I'm not going to go investigate and actually see where these studies are done. And there is no such studies that exist that demonstrate any of that. But there are studies: clear, the one I gave you. Nobody can refute a UN study, because the UN is obviously not a Muslim source. So nobody can refute a UN study which surveys tens of thousands of women in the Western America. So, if anyone has issues with abuse, I would say they should start with the West before they talk about any country.", "No sources, no numbers, no amount of people who were surveyed. Anyone can write anything. And this is just a random website. People can lie, anybody can lie. People need to understand how research is done. Research is not done by just some random person on Google writing something. That's not how you do research. You do research by investigating the process, the methodology of the research that took place, the number of people that participated, the questions that were asked and the locations, and the organisation that conducted the survey, because it could be a biased survey that is lying about the numbers. So once you do that, then you come to a conclusion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Left In Utter Shock After Attempting To Criticise Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cFKbacM6CFs", ((326, "5:26–6:05"), (369, "6:09–6:31"), (394, "6:34–7:35"), (477, "7:57–8:19"), (509, "8:29–9:25"), (585, "9:45–10:23"),))
