#passage(("Now, talking about the idea of marrying more than one: I'm going to say most women have a specific position. I believe most women, if they're in love with a person, they would never desire any other man. But that's not the case for men. And women cannot comprehend this, because they think if a man is attracted to another woman while he's in love with another woman, then he doesn't love her. The reason they think like this is because they can't comprehend this idea. But this is where we come to the idea of the difference and the rules being different, because we're different. Men and women are different. Therefore, the rules will be different for each of them.", "The women that will complain about marrying more than one are mostly the women that, let's say, for example, haven't been married before, or young in age. They would complain about that because it doesn't benefit them. But that same woman, if she got married, and then she spent, let's say, 7, 8 years with a man, and then she got divorced and now she's in her 30s, she would be more than happy of being a second wife to someone, cuz now she'll go to the man which is young, who is not married: \"Oh, marry me.\" \"Oh, look, but you already married once. Why do I have to marry you? I want someone who's young, who's not married like me.\" So these women that can be widows or divorcees, their position on being a second wife, third wife, fourth wife: women will be okay with it so long as it's in their benefit.", "That's why, even when people talk about prophet Muhammad marrying: all his wives except one were widows and [divorcees]. They were older in age, or widows and divorcees. So take looking after a wife which is a widow and a [divorcee], let's say as a second wife or whatever. She has kids; a man is looking after her. Why is that a problem? Why is that an issue?", "A lot of women, when they talk about this idea: why is it not allowed? Even if it was allowed, women wouldn't do it. But I'll tell you the