#passage(("First, Islam doesn't say go and marry the [widow]. You're rewarded if you do it, but it's not the only thing you could do.", "Whether that woman is beautiful is subjective anyways. He can come and tell you my first wife is more beautiful than my second wife. That's your own criteria. Younger, of course, that's an objective standard. Now the question is this: is he treating them fairly? So, a woman is okay being a second wife. It's consensual.", "Even if a man goes and marries the most beautiful woman on earth, doesn't change anything. It doesn't change the fact that still that man will die for you, protecting you when necessary; that man will take care of you together, and he will be just to both of you the same way Islamically, or he will be punished on the day of judgment. So none of this makes it unjust. Just because she's young and beautiful: this is a jealousy of women. \"Oh, she's more beautiful than me, she's younger than me\": it's just jealousy. But the woman that actually cares about women rights: \"You know what? I love women. This woman wants to get married. She's okay being a second wife. I love women. So, I'm for women's rights, so I'm okay. Marry another woman. Take care of another woman. She's also a woman.\" You should be a feminist. Be for the rights of women. The second woman wants to get married. Let's be for the rights of women. We love goodness for women.", "If he's not being just to her, she can separate from him. If he's being unjust to her, then in Islam, we have something called the divorce based on [harm]. She can go to a judge and she can be separated: he's not giving me my Islamic [rights]. Allah explicitly in the Quran says, \"Do not incline all the way towards one and leave the other one hanging.\" Allah explicitly in the Quran tells us not to do that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Grills Muslims On Equality Between Genders In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jmKBzsd6zsw", ((1514, "25:14–25:1