#passage(("Let's talk about other ideology. People say: oh, Islam is unjust to women because you're [allowed] to marry more than one wife. Let's say you are not a Muslim. Let's say you're an atheist. How many women can you be with? Let's look at things from non-Islamic lens. If I'm an atheist, how many women can I be with? What's the number? Let's remove the word marriage, which is useless in the west, because people are doing everything anyways and they just don't call it marriage. So can I live with a woman, have kids, and live in the same place? What is the limit?", "So why is nobody coming and complaining about the fact that people can have unlimited partners? And they already cheat, but it's not just cheating, but they also have the open relationships. And not only that, you have one way open relationship. You have men who are with women, and women are okay with this. The same women I'm talking about, they're okay being another side chick for a celebrity, for example. It just depend who's the man. If it's Leonardo DiCaprio, it's okay: I can be a side chick. I can be a number 14 on the list. I don't care, so long as I'm [seen] with him in public, I have a picture on my Instagram: oh, he's my boyfriend. So, if you're a rapper, you're a celebrity, whatever, it's okay for these women to be in a one-sided relationship where he has multiple women and she only has one. Maybe all of these celebrities in the west have multiple women on the side. They're married to one, but they have multiple women. And the wife knows, but they just keep it in secret. They don't publicize it, so they can save face for their wife. But they do it. And these women remain as wives.", "So as an atheist or a non-religious person, it's not morally wrong. I can have one open relationship. So long as the women are okay, every Westerner is going to be like: it's okay. So long as the women agree that you are in one-sided open relationship, it's okay and it's legal. But if it's a Muslim woman agreeing to be a second wife: no, no, no, that's wrong. Red light. We don't allow this. But it's the same thing. You can consensually be the number 14 side chick to a man, but oh, marrying another wife: no, no, it's bad, you're a Muslim, we don't allow you to do this. Big hypocrisy.", "What about other religions? You're not going to find any of the other major religions putting any restrictions on the number of wives you can have. You have Christians telling you can only marry one wife, but there is nothing in the book that says that. There's verses in the Old Testament says if he take another wife, then he should be good to the first one. So he's talking about having more than one wife. There's a legislation. And there's no limit. Remember, there's no limit. Doesn't say you can only marry this or that. Islam is the only one is limiting in this case.", "So we compare every other world ideology, because if someone wants to complain about Islam, then you must be something else. You must be Christian, Jewish, atheist. But in the end, all of these other ideologies is 10 times worse than whatever you're complaining about in Islam. And Islam has no issues.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Grills Muslims On Equality Between Genders In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jmKBzsd6zsw", ((729, "12:09–13:15"), (805, "13:25–14:39"), (884, "14:44–15:26"), (926, "15:26–16:14"), (974, "16:14–16:31"),))
// U ML123:98-217 | The Muslim Lantern | 8
#passage(("A lot of women, and our sisters in the West, and a lot of people generally, have grown up in a worldview based on, let's say, Hollywood movies, this and that. And it's based on this kind of \"charming prince\": the person is going to come and save the day, and put the ring on, and this type of party, whatever. And a lot of this is unrealistic. People in real life don't live that way. It's a movie for a reason! Things don't happen that way.", "So you see people, what they do is they blame Muslims. By the way, it's illegal for a Muslim, for example, in the UK, to marry more than a wife! Talking about legal marriage, you cannot marry more than one woman according to the law in the UK. But how many girlfriends can you have according to the UK law at the same time? Infinite. You have people having millions of partners. You heard of three ways, or whatever. All of these terms are happening in the West today. All of this is practised very normally.", "You get husbands married to their wives, cheating on their wives. Every time they travel, they go to a hotel. Just ask the hotel! Sometimes I talk to receptionists in hotels. Just ask them: how many husbands do you see here coming, and booking a night, and then bring in some... the type of women I'm referring to, I don't even want to say the name, but they bring these type of women, or they bring someone that they're cheating with, either way.", "We're going to be upfront, we're going to treat both of them equally, both of them are going to be aware that I'm getting married to the other woman, and everyone is in the picture, and it's a marriage under the eyes of God, and there are obligations and responsibilities. So you've got to give her her marital gift. You've got to take care of her. You've got to protect her. There are obligations that you need to do. You've got to have her own place that she's going to live in, in Islam. So instead of just having intercourse with her, like people do in the West, and throw her away and go to the next girl, Islam has a system! And when people say: we don't want to implement the system of Islam, then you come up with something else that is just corruption for society, like you see in the Western society.", "Now, some men are OK being monogamous. And I don't accept this idea that every man necessarily wants to marry more than one woman. I don't think it's necessarily true that every man desires that, or wants that. But there are many men that do. And especially that you got married to someone, you spent a very long time: now, the intimate dynamic is not the same after 15 years and 20 years of getting married and having children. It's not the same. So that can cause a bit of danger, because the desire that the husband has is not the same as the woman has. A woman will come to menopause. It's not going to be the same drive. So there are changes that are biological as well. So keeping all of that in mind, Allah knows that which is beneficial for each, for the man and for the woman.", "And also Allah has given rights to both of them. For example, a woman doesn't want to be a second wife. In Islam, before marriage, a woman, according to many schools of thought and many scholars, they would say she's allowed to type in the contract, in the marriage agreement: you're not allowed to marry another wife. And if he ever breaks that, then now she's allowed to separate from him, and she's allowed to keep her marital gift: مَهر (Mahr: marital gift) is basically material thing that he would give her, all of these things. She's allowed to keep all of that. But if she asks for separation without him doing anything wrong, she needs to give him back his marital gift. But in this case, because he broke the contract, she gets 2 privileges: to keep her marital gift, and to also in the same time separate from him, initiate the separation by going to a judge and saying: now I want to separate, he broke this rule. OK, that's it! The separation taking place between both of them. So Islam gives the women the right. Nobody here is forced to do anything.", "But a lot of women, and when I say \"a lot\", we don't mean the majority, but a lot of women are OK being second wives. Because, for example, some women cannot give birth. They cannot have children. So they're OK being either a second wife, or a first wife that allows another wife, so the husband can have children if he would like to have children in the future. There are women that are widows and divorcees that come from war-torn countries. For example, when the war in Syria happened, many Syrian women left, and they were OK being second wives, because they were coming from a war-torn country. They have children. They're in a new country. So there's many situations like this.", "And on top of that, you can just look at men and women generally in society, especially with the introduction of the LGBT movements and this and that. If every man marries a woman, there will be women that are left, that don't have anyone that they can marry. And there's no solution for that. So you're either going to keep these women alone, or you're going to accept the idea of a man being with more than one woman. Because generally in the West, there's more women than men.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Lady Questions A Muslim On Polygamy Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pL8KhAcUgn0", ((320, "5:20–5:42"), (356, "5:56–6:32"), (398, "6:38–6:56"), (423, "7:03–7:36"), (462, "7:42–8:25"), (506, "8:26–9:25"), (565, "9:25–10:03"), (606, "10:06–10:28"),))
