#passage(("In reality, whether a lot of women like it or not, women are OK sharing their partner. I'm not saying all of them, but I'm saying there are many women that are. Men, on average, are not, though, on the other hand, because it's an attack on their manhood, in a sense, if they think that \"Oh, I'm going to share my woman\". They say 'my woman'; they look at it that way. But women... That's why you have a second and third wife. Why do you have a second and third wife? Because that second wife is a woman! And that third wife is a woman! And she's OK being a second wife and a third wife. That can happen; Allah has left that in the nature.", "But what you need to understand is, that is, in the end, a choice for the woman. But there are women that are OK and want to be second wives. They see a man, they like that man a lot, they believe they're not going to easily find a man like that, and he's married. And they're OK even if they're going to be a second wife, as long as they are with that person. So why do we prohibit that right of these other women that want to get married? Why?", "What do you mean by fun? If you mean by fun that a man wants to have intercourse with a woman, that's the whole reason men get married. If you go to a man and say you're not allowed to have intercourse with this woman, they're not going to marry her! It's not \"fun\", this is the point I'm making: it's a marriage. It's something that you do under the eyes of God; it's a revered tradition. It's not just a game! Also, there are responsibilities in marriage; that's the difference.", "So, the people in the West are OK by men going and using women like sexual objects, moving from one to another. Islam says you have to treat them equally; if you don't, you don't get married to more than one wife (AnNisa4:3). You have to treat them equally. That means everything you do for this woman, in your power, you need to do it to the other woman. You give the same amount of time to this woman as you give to that woman. But in the West, they're OK: this man goes and sleeps around day and night, and he spends his life with hundreds of partners, and he brags about how many bodies he has, and nobody complains about this! They accept it as a part of their culture and community, and that's the problem! People are attacking marriage, which is a revered tradition from God, and they don't have any issue with perversions in societies and hedonism that people are living in.", "So in Islam, there's no such thing as \"for fun\", because when you get married, you have obligations: protection and provision and all of these things. And you're responsible towards the family of the wife, as her family now knows your family, and all of that comes in the picture. It's marriage! While having intercourse with a girl you meet one night, they say \"one night stand\": use this girl one night and then go to the next one. Nobody knows anything, nobody hears anything, and then that's it. I find it very hypocritical from people in the West when they highlight things like that, especially if many people in their past, they've had multiple boyfriends. But it's an issue if we say that a man is going to have more than one wife. Why?! It's the same thing. But the only difference is he's actually given the rights to the wife, and he's honestly doing it, he's taking care of both of them, and he's not lying to his wife.", "They're not offering a solution; it does happen in the end. And these families are destroyed and people get divorced; this is the outcome that takes place. Rather than being upfront, because he can't come to his wife and say, I want another wife. He can't! The woman will divorce the husband, and she'll take half his money, and take his children and all of that. So he's going to cheat. His only option is to cheat. While in Islam, you don't need to cheat, because your wife already knows that this is something allowed in Islam, and if she has a problem with that, she has the right to, in the beginning, make that clear. But if she doesn't make that clear, then that option remains available. So they're not the same at all; they're completely different.", "In Islam, it's not only he's committing a Major Sin, there's a Capital Punishment waiting for him. There's no jokes. You cannot just go and do adultery. Adultery in Islam is punishable by death. So, while in the West you can do this in the clubs, you cannot do this in an Islamic society, because that destroys families.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Wife Grills A Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tUX4xfgST_E", ((795, "13:15–13:47"), (830, "13:50–14:51"), (961, "16:01–16:38"), (1016, "16:56–17:51"), (1078, "17:58–18:45"), (1185, "19:45–20:58"), (1269, "21:09–21:24"),))
