#passage(("You can't have intercourse with a woman outside marriage. That's the only situation Islamically where you're allowed to do it. This disease that starts with the P word exists only in western societies, because western societies allow intercourse prior to marriage. In Islam you're not allowed to have, not only intercourse, you're not allowed to touch a woman! That is not lawful for you!", "The 'Idda itself is the waiting period, until the woman is able to engage in marriage again. Also the 'Idda for the person divorced would be the period where the husband can take the wife back without a new marriage contract, can take her back with telling her, \"I took her back\", or by other means the scholars talk about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions Muslim On Young Marriages Then Instantly Regrets It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zHZPZujQbd8", ((669, "11:09–11:32"), (765, "12:45–12:59"),))
