#passage(("They're physically not a child anymore. But you're talking about the mental maturity.", "Now the question is: does the father know if his daughter is mentally ready to get married or not? Does anyone else know better and care better about his own daughter than the father? Obviously not. So we say in this case the father is going to look at the girl, and in this day and age, I would say 99%, it's really impossibility that she would be mentally ready; then he would wait. If he will marry her at the age of nine and she's not ready yet psychologically, and that will cause her harm, then this is unacceptable Islamically.", "You cannot just go around and do whatever you want to your daughters. She's not like sheep or something. So that marriage is a very exceptional case. The dad now has to present a case: why does he want to get his daughter married so early? What's the reason? I give you an example: that was the prophet of God, and you want to make sure that your daughter marries the prophet of God. You don't want to lose that. Now in an everyday situation, you go to the father and say: why are you trying to marry your girl so young? What's the reason behind it? What's the benefit in doing that? Is that good for the girl? No. If she's still nine, she cannot even comprehend the world, and you're going to give her to some stranger man? No. Then you're not doing it for her benefit; then it's not allowed. Also the girl's acceptance is a part of it as well. So it's not only that she has a guardian, but the girl has to approve. She cannot just be forced.", "Today this doesn't happen in Muslim society, Muslim community. It doesn't happen. Also, the culture back then was very different. Aisha, before Prophet Muhammad, she was already engaged to one of the people in the community. So this was not the prophet doing something out of [the ordinary]. Girls don't go to kindergarten. You just reach puberty, you're ready to have kids, you're ready to get married. That's how societies looked at women and females at that time. So it's a complete different society.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Shocked By Muslim After Questioning The Prophet's Marriage! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SxG2d79W6j0", ((742, "12:22–12:26"), (793, "13:13–13:48"), (848, "14:08–15:06"), (922, "15:22–16:00"),))
