#passage(("What's the problem with cousin marriages? How much does the chance really increase? It increases by 1 to 2%. So if the argument is: just because we have an exception, 1 to 2%, in which defects may appear, therefore we have to say that cousin marriages are wrong, let's try now to apply this rule. For instance, women that are post the age of 40, what is the chance for them to have a child with autism, if they're past the age of 40 and they have a child? It's like 80% more likely, or something, than if the woman is not past. So should we say now, since women past the age of 40 have this likelihood, then women that pass the age of 40 should not have kids?", "Now we can apply this to obesity. The chances of autism and all other diseases: if a woman is obese, if a woman has high blood pressure, if a woman has high sugar, all of them will increase even more than the percentage if we talk about cousin marriages. So if this rule were to be applied, someone comes and says, \"Oh, the percentages increase with 1%, therefore we say we shouldn't do this\", then we will have to apply this rule to every case in which the percentages of harm can increase to the children, even a lot more, which would be actually most people having children at this point. Look at the obesity today. Look at people with health problems, blood pressure, high sugar, women over the age of 40. We will have to prevent everybody from having kids at this point.", "For example, we say: I'm not going to become a doctor, because there is a 5% chance of me getting infection if I'm going to treat person who has a disease, covid for example. Nobody should be a doctor because there's a chance of infection? We start applying this: oh, there's a very small chance of harm happening to you, therefore that specific thing should not be done. Now that's a huge issue. By the way, we can apply this to anything, like car crashes, plane crashes. There's this small percentage of a possibility of a car crash: okay, don't get on planes, don't drive cars.", "Now also there's genetic ways to check: if you're worried you're going to marry your cousin, you can both do research and check if you have it so close that it increases the likelihood or not, because it's not just about being a cousin, but it's to do with the genetics of the two individuals. So today we can also do this. Allah in the Quran tells us to ask the people of knowledge if we're afraid of any harm; that's not against Islam, to go and ask and do research.", "We got to also talk about the idea of time and place, the Sharia, because even we're saying we can do these things genetically today, we could not have done them in the past, and the laws of Allah have to be applicable for every day and time and place. And there are more benefits of allowing cousin marriages than harms. There's many benefits. There is many tribes, for example, that have this tradition, many tribes that have the tradition of closely only marrying between each other. Love and attachment and connection can happen between cousins, and it can develop, and that can lead them to do something very harmful, which is disobeying God and doing fornication or doing adultery, due to the fact that this thing is not allowed, because you can be around your cousin or your family member, and you can develop attachment, you can develop feelings. You're a human being in the end. So for someone to say: let Islam close this door because there's a very very small percentage of something happening, is not reasonable in any way, shape or form. Let us leave all of these benefits, that are a lot more than the harms, because there's a small percentage that can be applicable to any topic in life?", "Many scholars in Islam recommended that you marry from the further, the better it is. It's more recommended. It is better that the individuals marry further away. Now this is something very important here. If I say something is allowed, it does not mean that I'm saying I'm encouraging it. Just because Islam says it is allowed to marry, Islam is not saying you should marry. [Makruh] is where something is allowed, but if you do it you don't get a sin, but if you leave it you get a reward. However, in this case, I'm saying scholars would recommend that you get married further away rather than to get married closer. This is a recommendation of many scholars. However, the point I'm making is Islam is not encouraging the idea. It's not saying do it, but it's allowing it, because there is more benefit, like I mentioned, for all of these cultural things and societal things. And it's a door that shouldn't be closed because there's an exception that is small, applicable in this case to things that are even a lot more, like obesity or past the age of 40.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Agnostic Grills Muslim On Cousin Marriage And Racism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fvVrT_WHQxg", ((2126, "35:26–37:18"), (2238, "37:18–38:06"), (2296, "38:16–38:56"), (2341, "39:01–39:30"), (2379, "39:39–40:47"), (2454, "40:54–42:27"),))

