#passage(("With marriage in Islam, a man can marry only two people who are not Muslim, which is Christian or Jewish, not any woman. So if a woman is atheist, polytheist like a Hindu woman, you're not allowed to marry her.", "Now these Christian and Jewish women as well, there's conditions that many people don't know. First, for example, she has to believe in her book. Other than believing in her book, she also has to be [chaste], meaning either she's a virgin or she doesn't sleep around.", "Now you say: Okay, can a Muslim woman marry a Christian man or a Jewish man who believes in his book and he's [chaste]? No. Reason being is because the head of the household is the man, and an outcome of that is that the children will follow the religion of the father.", "We don't say that's why the rule is there. We say the rule is there because Allah commanded it. One wisdom we can see, which some Scholars have mentioned, is that, but not only that. I'll give you an example. In Islam we fast Ramadan. Fasting is not just eating and drinking; fasting is also having intercourse. Now you're not going to expect a man who's not a Muslim to wait for a Muslim woman for a period of a month, not having intercourse with her. The desires that men have is not the same as the woman. Someone who's not a Muslim and he's married to a woman which is a Muslim, now he says: this is my wife, I want to have intercourse with my wife today, why you expect me to wait?", "I'm talking in reality. You expect or you want that your partner respects your views. I don't disagree with that, but I'm saying in reality, in most cases, is the man going to listen or is he going to behave based on his desires? Allah does not make rules based on exceptions. We look at the majority. Are majority of women influenced by their partner? Yes, they are. Are majority of children following the religion of the father? Yes.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Feminist Confronts A Muslim On Gender Equality! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i9Sjr47uJyo", ((104, "1:44–1:58"), (118, "1:58–2:26"), (157, "2:37–2:56"), (203, "3:23–4:21"), (274, "4:34–5:07"),))
// U ML284:579-697 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("There are people committing Zina through marriage! You know how they're committing Zina through marriage? They are marrying people that are not lawful for them. So it's not marriage in Islam. They're committing Zina. They go to women in the West and marry these women, and they say they're \"Christian\" women.", "Did Allahﷻ allow the Muslim to marry a Christian or a Jew? Yes! So Allahﷻ allowed the Muslim to marry a Christian. What am I talking about then? Allahﷻ have put 2 conditions; without these two conditions your marriage is not permissible. Where did Allah put them? In the same verse that he allowed you to do. Open Surat alMaida (5:5). In the same verse Allah says: وَٱلۡمُحۡصَنَٰتُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ. After he said: أُحِلَّ لَكُمُ (Made permissible for you), he said: وَٱلۡمُحۡصَنَٰت. What does مُحصَنة mean? In the Arabic language مُحصَنة means the chaste, pure woman. So the woman either has to be a virgin, or she has repented if she did something in the past, and she does not sleep around with anyone. She does not do these things. And we have evidence she's repented, now she doesn't do these things. There are Christian women that actually preserve their chastity. You can count them probably on your hand in every city, but there are Christian women who tend to do that. They exist, but they're certainly nowhere near even close to be the majority.", "And then He said: مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ (She believes in her book, she's given the Book, she believes in the Scripture). You come to the women of today: Are you Christian? \"Yes.\" Do you believe in the Bible? \"No, I don't believe in all of these things!\" Why are you Christian then? You believe Jesus is God? \"I don't follow religion, religion has been made by men!\" But what do you mean by Christian? \"Yes, my father.. I was baptised when I was 10.. He put me in the water and Khalas! (That's it!)\" So do you believe in the Book? \"No! I don't believe in religion but I'm \"Christian\".\" They go marry these women. So he's effectively not married there, he's committing Zina under Islamic Shari'a rules. This is not marriage, because that woman is an Atheist, Deist, Agnostic. She's not a Believer! So they think they have married.", "And you got women as well. Because women as well have a big problem; don't think it's just the men. The men have this problem. The women, what problem do they have? The women have the problem of completely marrying Kuffar now: Atheist, Agnostic, Christian, Jew. It's not permitted for them. Nowhere in the Quran it is permitted for a woman to marry even from the Jews or the Christians. It's not permissible; Allah did not allow the woman to do that. Allah explicitly prohibits that in the Quran (alBaqara2:221). Allah says: وَلَعَبۡدٞ مُّؤۡمِنٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّن مُّشۡرِكٖ (A slave, a believing slave is better than Mushrik). Allah says in the Quran as well in (alMumtahana60:10), what does He say? فَلَا تَرۡجِعُوهُنَّ إِلَى ٱلۡكُفَّارِۖ (Do not return them to the Kuffar) لَا هُنَّ حِلّٞ لَّهُمۡ (they're [Muslim women] not permissible for them) وَلَا هُمۡ يَحِلُّونَ لَهُنَّۖ (and they're [non-Muslim men] not permissible for them). Can it be clearer than this? This is like the Sun.", "But the women, they still go. I find the women coming from somewhere in Asia, Indonesia, Malaysia, or whatever it is, Thailand. Are you Muslim? Yes, Muslim. And he's Muslim? No. How are you together?! And they come with babies, pushing them with the trolley. And you want to think: how this woman lives with someone like this? How does she live? Because that man comes at the end of the night drunk. His children, he teaches them his values of drinking Alcohol, and going to the clubs and bars. You don't know how she lives with someone like this! We do not want to talk about things which will be Offensive, to do with وضوء (Wudu': Ablutions) and غسل (Ghusl: Purification); we do not even want go to that extent, but imagine there: How do you live with someone like this? This is the marriage through Zina.", "And there is the normal Zina. In the amount I've been doing Da'wa, I can not tell you the number of boyfriends and girlfriends that I've seen that one is Muslim and one is not Muslim: Muslim girl and a non-Muslim boy, or a non-Muslim girl with a Muslim boy. And every time I see it, until this day, I get angry. It doesn't matter how many times I see it, I get angry. Especially when it's a sister, I get more angry. And I'm like: SubhanAllah, if these are the Muslims I'm seeing on a day, what's going on here? What is the difference between a Believer and a Disbeliever? What is the distinction? If we are going to live effectively a very similar life, then what is the difference between us? Why are you using that title \"Muslim\" for yourself? Where is that Islam?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((2060, "34:20–34:34"), (2080, "34:40–35:44"), (2156, "35:56–36:48"), (2208, "36:48–37:45"), (2271, "37:51–38:54"), (2334, "38:54–39:43"),))
