#passage(("The simple reason: Allahﷻ said so; he allowed it, therefore it's allowed. But the Jew and the Christian women: first, the main and most important reason is Allahﷻ commanded it. Now what's the wisdom? Some Scholars have spoken about it. For example, the fact that we are very close to the Christian and Jewish women in their beliefs. So we believe in the same Prophets, most of the same Prophets; we believe in the Hellfire and Heaven. The commands, most of them are similar; we have the commonalities between the Prophets and all of these different things. So it's very easy for a woman, if she lives with a Muslim man, to accept Islam, to become a Muslim in the future. That's a very easy thing, because there's already a lot of communalities between you and that woman. And even if she doesn't, the children will follow the religion of the father. The father is the leader of the household, therefore the children will follow his example.", "If we flip the roles now, and a woman is a Muslim and she's with a non-Muslim man, he will enforce his own views on the children; he's the leader of the household. And also he will influence her ideas and her understanding, which is very natural. So there again it all comes back to this idea: if you put it in your mind, men and women are not the same, therefore treatment with them has to be different. Then these ideas become much easier to understand when you look at the nature of a man and the nature of woman.", "For example, when it comes to intercourse and things done in the intercourse, how the intercourse is done, there are many things that are prohibited from an Islam perspective. That man would say: \"I don't care what your religion says, I want to do this\", \"I don't care if your religion says this specific act cannot be done in this way\". He doesn't care, he wants to enjoy himself, this is his wife. So it's very problematic.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Lady Questions Muslim About Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", 