#passage(("Chapter 5 of Quran, verse 5, clearly stipulates that Muslim men specifically, not women, are allowed to marry a Jewish or a Christian woman. But a Jewish or a Christian woman, she has to be chaste, meaning not necessarily she has to be a virgin, but she's a woman that doesn't go around having intercourse with men. She doesn't commit fornication, because fornication even in Christianity and Judaism is not allowed. It's not just in Islam; people don't follow, but these are the teachings.", "So all Muslim women you are allowed to marry, obviously the ones that are not married and etc., and not your family members, and Christian or Jews women with these two conditions.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “If You Answer My QUESTIONS I will Accept Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C2LVHjA4HbM", ((846, "14:06–14:31"), (876, "14:36–14:51"),))
