#passage(("Muslims are allowed to marry from the People of the Book. So, Muslims are allowed to marry Christians and Jews. But the important thing is that now, if you know something is the Truth, then it's very important for you to tell other people about the Truth as well, and you care about your wife. That goes without saying, so you want goodness for her. You do not want her to worship other than Allah, you do not want her to blaspheme or worship a human being and die upon something which is false.", "But the important thing is this: before worrying about others, you should be worrying about yourself. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Oh, you who believe! قُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَكُمْ) protect yourself, then your families from the fire (Attahrim66:6). Because if I'm not myself protected, then how can I protect other people from the fire? So, the important thing is you taking the step yourself first: entering into the fold of the religion, following the practices and the teachings, gaining knowledge bit by bit, and while you're doing that, also telling your wife about Islam, telling her about Jesus, telling her about these very basic things. Also, you're welcome to bring her for someone who is knowledgeable about the religion to talk to her about Christianity, if she's got any questions. Maybe she's worried about this or that. Someone can explain to her why Jesus cannot be God, and why the Bible is changed and all of these things.", "So, if a person is sincere, then have no worry: Allah will guide them eventually, because they're sincere and they're looking for the Truth. If you're sincere, looking for the Truth, then Allah will guide you. So, it will be the same thing with your wife, with your family, with everyone else. But it's a gradual process as well and it will require patience. Allah is going to test you sometimes with patience. It might not happen straight away; they might struggle a bit with it, they might be disagreeing with you. It's not going to be as easy as \"Ok, there is Islam.\" and then they say, \"We become Muslim!\" As it was a process for you, it will be a process for them as well. But as long as you're doing things correctly and as long as they are sincere, Allah will guide them. There's no doubt about that.", "But first, you have to work on yourself by accepting Islam and then learning bit by bit about the prayer. You can take your time. As long as you're putting the effort, Allah will reward you, and there is no sin on you until you completely learn how to pray, and then, the next step, you start learning about the other thing. So, Islam is like this: It's a gradual process that starts from A and then ends with Z. You cannot jump from A to Z straight away. You have to take things step by step, bit by bit, and then you move forward.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Asks God For A Sign Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HhJvhr8ihyY", ((309, "5:09–5:29"), (333, "5:33–6:10"), (378, "6:18–7:01"), (422, "7:02–7:24"),))
