#passage(("Then they will also talk about divorce, for example. They will say that divorce is always in the hand of the man; the man can divorce whenever he wants. That's false. As a man, you cannot divorce if your woman is menstruating. You cannot divorce if you had intercourse in purity with your wife. So, you have menstruation, purity, impurity. If I had intercourse, I cannot divorce her within that purity. I have to wait for her to become pure again and not have intercourse with her in that purity. Then I can divorce her. Why? Isn't it a religion made to suit the desire of the man? Why is it restricting me?", "And for the woman, you have something called khula, where you can separate from the man. We have cases in the Sunnah where a woman, she was not attracted to a man and she was separated from him. So, khula can be done from your side without the agreement of the man. You have something called talaq al-darar, which is a divorce of harm. If the man is doing anything harmful to you, you're able to do that type of divorce, and even though if the man doesn't agree, you're separated from him.", "But Allah understands the nature of the woman. Allah understands that woman goes through stages and emotions, and she might say something, \"Divorce me,\" when she's in a stage where her emotions are here or there, and she doesn't mean it, and she regrets it later. So, there is a process, so we make sure that she's fully balanced, she knows what she's doing, she's making that decision that she's not going to come and regret in the future. So, it's about honoring the nature of the woman. Islam honors the nature of the woman by understanding the nature of the woman.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is Islam A Religion Made For The Men?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OzxyEO708yI", ((948, "15:48–16:16"), (977, "16:17–16:38"), (998, "16:38–17:07"),))
// U ML038:596-666 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Who relies more on emotions, the men or the women? The women, who goes through menstrual cycle throughout the month, and the PMS and all of these things, where their hormones change, and they will say something and the next day they'll like: I never said this. Is that a natural thing that all women go through? Now if the woman goes through these stages, who do you think is easier to say the word divorce, the men or the women? So when a woman is in that stage, she goes like: divorce me, divorce. They don't say I divorce, because Allah didn't give them that. But they say their favorite word: divorce me. They say 24/7. The reason the man doesn't divorce them is because he knows that she's being emotional right now. Then next day she comes, she hugs: I love you, this and that. Yesterday she was saying divorce me, but this is how women are.", "Allah knows the men and women. This is what you need to put in your mind: this idea of feminism, you're going to take it, put it in the bin, because it's incorrect. What you need to do is to understand men and women are different, and if men and women are different, then since women go through these stages and through these phases, Allah will give them something that works for them. If Allah gave them the right of divorce, we're going to have everybody divorced in society.", "Let's compare the idea in the west. In America, for example, men and women can initiate divorce. If men and women can initiate divorce, who do you think is initiating more divorce, men or women, in the west? So you have these nearly 50% divorce rate or whatever. I have 80% of women initiating the divorce, and a lot of it is no fault divorce. It's not like the guy did something bad, or just like: oh, it's my mood in the day, it's my emotional stage right now, I'm going to divorce. So you see already the application, when you allow this idea, what it leads to. So if it's more than 80% of women doing it, then we understand that if you open this door, then you have a society with barely people married. Look at the west now, with all single women and single men. Then you have 90% of criminals in the prison, they're coming from single parent homes. You're completely destroying your society. You can think small rule. It's not a small rule. The creator has commanded that for a reason.", "So that's the first thing. The man doesn't go through that stage. So he is going to be calculated in his decision. Also, the man has a financial liability. If he divorces the woman, the woman keeps her marital gift. So, she's winning in that case by keeping her marital gift. He loses that marital gift and he loses the woman. So, he's got to calculate: I married that woman. Now, do I want to divorce the woman?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Grills Muslims On Equality Between Genders In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jmKBzsd6zsw", ((1941, "32:21–33:33"), (2017, "33:37–33:58"), (2042, "34:02–35:02"), (2102, "35:02–35:28"),))
// U ML236:990-1012 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The laws to do with the marriage, with the husband and the wife, to do with the children, with the family structures, giving each of them laws, and we see the opposite of that today! America is a prime example: 50-50 partnership, feminism, all of these things. Look at the community today: women into the workforce, no longer the man is a provider. You see here society is completely in destruction!", "Islam says: not giving the divorce to women, but giving them خُلع (khul'), which is a completely different thing, where they have to give back their marital gift. But the idea is that divorce as an action is given primarily to the man. There's a sense of separation that a woman can do, but with certain conditions. But mainly it's for the man.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((3232, "53:52–54:13"), (3259, "54:19–54:32"),))
