#passage(("There's also cases in Islam in which, for example, there's a companion woman that came to the [prophet]. She married a man, a companion. Then she came to the prophet: I do not have any criticism of his manners, I don't have any criticism of his religion. So he's a good person. But the only thing: I fear that I cannot fulfill my right towards him. Let's say she's not attracted to him; she's not going to be able to fulfill her right. She came to the [prophet]. Then the prophet asked her, \"Would you give him back his garden?\" He gave her as a marital gift a full garden. He's a good mannerful person. He's a good religious person. He doesn't have any bad characteristics. You want to divorce? Would you give him back his garden? She said, \"Yes.\" The prophet said to him, \"Take your garden back and divorce him.\" Even though he wasn't doing anything, she was not attracted to him in that way. That is also found in Islam.", "But this idea of feminism is that which ruined, it's not only ruined the West, it's ruining the whole world at this point. Go look at how western families are. Go look at these women crying day and night. They have no spouses. They're being used and abused every day and night. She's coming complaining about Islam, this rule and that rule. But these rules don't exist in the West at all. There's no rules. You can do whatever you want. So isn't that more worthy of criticizing than coming talking about Islam, which given you these wise rules from the creator that knows what benefits you and what works for the nature of a woman and what works for the nature of the man? Once you understand, it's not like we not treated the same; because we're not the same. Women are one way, men are one way, and God gives them that which is wise and more beneficial for them.", "Of course they're upset. Of course there's a disagreement happening. But it's a calculated decision. The person can be angry, can be upset, but it's a calculated decision: the man knows in