#passage(("The more time went by, the more I realized this is becoming a really serious issue. And I'm sorry to say this, but I have no doubt that the overwhelming majority, sadly, if you are a parent, there is something you're doing wrong in your parenting. It's something sad to say, because we have all the guidance. We have all the means. We have all the ability. The Islam has given us the guidance; we can understand and know what we need to do, what is the right approach that we take with our kids. But most parents are not doing this. This is a serious issue. It's not something which is small here and there.", "I've always been getting emails from people, sometimes with doubts, sometimes with issues. But recently, I'm realizing there's more and more parents who would reach out and say: \"My kid left Islam. Kid became a different religion.\" Or \"My kid just left the religion of Islam, became an atheist, became a liberal. My daughter is joining the rainbow flag movement. My son is doing this.\" And this is becoming more and more. It is not something that is happening and disappearing and these kids are coming back to the religion. No, this is increasing and increasing on and on every day. And people book private sessions with me sometimes, and I've noticed this also increasing in the private sessions. People would book a private session about their son, about their daughter, for me to talk to them. Recently, someone had a kid that became a Christian, and I had an entire 2-hour discussion with them. They left Christianity, but now they're atheists. \"I don't know what happened to them. They were okay, and one day, they left Islam.\" No, it's never like this.", "I recently had another private session, just like last week or a few days ago, with parents crying and talking about how they realize now how they should have done so many things that they were not doing, that this is their responsibility. But you don't want to be that person. You don't want to be the parent