#passage(("Why is the Fitna of Shubuhat, the Fitna of doubts, more severe than the Fitna of Shahawat, desires? It is because the Fitna of Shubuhat leads the person to leaving Islam! The person encounters doubts, especially in these days and age living in the West. You are a Muslim, you go to the university, you find in the university there is free mixing, men with women, and if you do not engage in that free mixing, what do you become? You become the alienated individual, the person who is like a Stranger. Why are you doing this? Everyone else is free mixing; they are looking at you like a stranger: why you are not doing the same thing that everyone else is doing? Woman puts her hand to shake your hand at the University. We've got a big issue now. Should you shake your hand and compromise your Deen (Religion)? Or be labelled as the Muslim extremist? Why are you extreme? Because, how can you not shake the hand of a woman when she puts her hand? Do you think she's less than you! That's their understanding: if you don't shake hands, therefore you're inferior.", "So, as a Muslim you tend to come across these problems, you feel alienated, in the University, or in your workplace, the same problems. You're not able to shake hands, people are mixing, people are eating food, they're talking about certain things that oppose your religion. Not only that: when you go to university, when you are listening to professors and teachers, they intentionally want to instil doubt within you, especially the students, whether it is in School or Universities.", "In the Western Community, if you put your children in school, if you put them in a mixed disbelieving school, be prepared that one day they might come to you and say: I'm not a Muslim anymore. I have met, personally doing دعوة (Da'wa: Invitation to Islam), a child who is roughly from 7 to 8 or 9 years old. Do you know what he said? He said: \"I'm an Atheist.\" I was like \"What!?\" 7 year old child! The kid is like this, you barely can see him, and he said to me: \"I'm an Atheist\"! He didn't just say I'm an Atheist and not understanding the meaning of what he's saying, because you can be a child, you hear a word and you repeat that word. In fact I asked him: \"What do you mean by Atheist? You don't believe there's God?\" He said: \"Yes, I don't believe there's God.\" Then I said to him: \"OK, there's a table here; where did this table come from? Didn't someone make it? Who makes the universe?\" He said: \"No, I'm an Atheist\", and his face changed, and he left, and he hid behind his mother. Can you imagine! He is not just an Atheist; he is someone who firmly believes in his Atheism. The kid is 7 years old!", "Now I want to ask you this question, people who have children here: if I get your 7 year old son, would he respond in the same way about being a Muslim? If I were to question him about the teachings of Islam, and I were to tell him: are you Muslim? You sure? And I ask him some questions about Allah, would he get upset that I'm questioning him about his beliefs, and then turn away and move away from me? If the answer is \"No\", then we have a huge problem today, we have a huge issue.", "What I've not told you in the story: he was the son of someone who is a Muslim; he is not a son of an Atheist. This is a real event that happened a few weeks ago; I even tweeted about it. This person is a Muslim. But do you know what happened? He was married to a non-Muslim woman, \"Christian\". One daughter he had, the elder daughter, was about 10, 11 years old, roughly this age, and she said: \"I don't know, I'm Agnostic.\" So, a Muslim father, married to a non-Muslim woman, with an Atheist child, and an Agnostic daughter at 10 years old! This are the fruits that some Muslims are producing in the West. They're producing the next generation of Atheists and Agnostics, that come to me on the same Da'wah table and engage with me, debate with me about why Atheism is the Truth and why Islam is false. And these are the lineage of Muslims!", "So, we need to know what is happening, we need to know why are these things happening. This 7 years old child, no one can come and tell me he came to that conclusion on his own: a 7 years old child happened to come to the conclusion that Atheism is the Truth, and that there is no God, and the table came from nothing! No, his teacher in the University, his teacher in the school, his teacher in the kindergarten, have taught him these values. I have another friend, and that friend, his wife came with one of her children, and her daughter, she goes to the kindergarten, and she was saying: \"Jesus died for our sins!\" I was like: \"What's going on here, what's happening here!\" And then she's debating, arguing: \"No, actually Jesus died for our sins.\" These are things that are being taught to children today.", "These are some of the diseases that are inflicting this Ummah today. So the Fitna of Shubuhat, why we're saying is more dangerous? Is because of what I'm telling you. You're putting doubt in the heart of someone, whether it is about the Truthfulness of Islam, whether it's about God's existence, whether it's about any topic, whatever the topic is. You're putting doubts in the heart of that person, and that person ends up being an Atheist, a Christian, a Jew, whatever it is. He leaves Islam, and the outcome of that is what? Is eternal Hellfire! This is something that there's no compromise here: the end result of someone who doesn't follow the teachings of Islam and doesn't die as a Muslim, he ends up in Hellfire. That is why that Fitna is more dangerous than committing sins. We're not saying you can commit sin as a Muslim in the West. But we're saying what is more dangerous.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((178, "2:58–3:55"), (239, "3:59–4:25"), (272, "4:32–5:38"), (346, "5:46–6:08"), (372, "6:12–7:15"), (442, "7:22–8:07"), (492, "8:12–9:01"),))
