#passage(("So, the number one reason and the biggest disease that I need to highlight is the idea of social media. Now, a lot of parents, cuz they're lazy parents, what do they do? You have parents, sometimes both parents working, or sometimes not both of them working. Sometimes you have multiple kids. The mother or father, you don't want to spend time and talk to the kids and do this and do that: Okay, here you go. There's your iPad. Go play. And in their mind, that's the solution: if I give the kid the iPad 2, 3, 4 hours, the kid is going to be busy playing with the iPad, and me, I'm going to have all the time in the world to cook, to clean, to do what I want, to go watch something, to relax. But it's never a harmless thing, like you're just giving the kid a device and that's the end of it. The iPad, iPhone, phone, whatever it is, is one of the main reasons for the destruction of the mentality of these kids. First, you destroy their mentalities, where you make them hooked to these devices and objects, where they're no longer social. Their entire life is on a device: on the computer, on the phone, like yourself. A lot of us are guilty of that. Now you're transmitting this problem and disease to your kids. Now they're hooked to live a life on a device. Everything they do: they wake up on a device, they sleep on a device. Now what's on this device? Social media. And parents have no restrictions. They see nothing, what this kid goes and watches.", "I was in a colleague's house once, someone I used to work with. I visited his house; he invited me. I think it was Ramadan or something. I sat in the living room, and his kid was sitting. There was a computer in a corner; it was the living room. And his father was there. We were talking. His father went to bring the food and come back. His kid was pretending to play some sort of a random game on the computer. The minute his father left, he started opening YouTube, and he was watching one of those YouTubers. I'm not going to