#passage(("There's so many stories I can talk about on kids mixing with other kids in school. And not just kids, but they even mix with other family members. You can have your kids mixing with your cousins. But the other family, which is your sister's family or your brother's family, they don't teach their kids any values. They're a liberal Muslim family or whatever. Their kids are going to have the wrong ideas, and these ideas are going to be transmitted to your kids. So, even if you home school your kids, even your own family members: what kind of kids are there that your kids are communicating?", "I noticed myself the lazy parents that just bring some random teacher: \"Oh, come. This random teacher is going to teach you Quran.\" No, you have to put the effort. I know when I was younger, if my parents take me to some teacher or whatever, I used to go there for the sake, because only my parents is telling me to go there. And I don't pay attention to what he's saying. Sometimes I don't attend, if I can escape it somehow. Don't care. You're just going there because your parents is telling you to do it. If you don't do it yourself, if you don't do it the right way, your kids are going to end up in the end in that path that I'm telling you, that we don't want any of our kids to end up in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “If You're Doing This, There's A Chance Your Kid Leaves Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r632sKczYqY", ((745, "12:25–12:55"), (793, "13:13–13:47"),))

