 simply, we're saying our beliefs and why we believe it from an Islamic religious perspective. And we don't believe in violence; we believe in telling people what is right and what is wrong, and that doesn't mean we would force our ideas with violence. We don't believe in that. So because some people think what I'm saying equals that you can be violent or behave towards these people differently: no! I'll behave with them just like any other human being that I know. I will speak to them with love, with care and everything, because I want guidance for them just like I want guidance for everyone else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((1042, "17:22–17:46"), (1071, "17:51–19:07"), (1152, "19:12–19:46"), (1219, "20:19–21:10"), (1278, "21:18–22:18"), (1344, "22:24–23:03"), (1385, "23:05–23:45"),))

