#passage(("You're making an assumption that homosexuality is an innate thing within human beings. So let's talk about this scientifically. What evidence do you have for that? Where are the studies that have been done to demonstrate what you're saying?", "Homosexuals are the minority in every scenario and in the human population, so they're not large. That's the first thing. The second thing is there are people who are paedophiles, who are everything else, and they are the same thing; they are a group of the people in society and they claim it's innate. Some people say I don't have control of being a paedophile or not. That does not mean that we would say it is an innate thing.", "You said it's an innate thing because there is a group of people who do it. How do you know they've not been conditioned? They are conditioned by society. You've not lived with them, you don't know their life story. You just know the end of what they tell you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Gay Student Confronts Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XqXTdyMc3OU", ((311, "5:11–5:29"), (342, "5:42–6:01"), (380, "6:20–6:47"),))
// U ML378:307-342 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("For example, Robert Spitzer is someone who's called the Father of Modern psychology in America. He's a Scientist, he's the Father of Modern Psychology. You can google him and you have a Wikipedia page popping up for you. Because he's well known, they have all the information about him. So, Robert Spitzer conducted a study, which was published in Nature Magazine, where he brought 200 homosexuals.", "By the way, he was attacked for his research, proving my point that there is a specific worldview in the Western society, and it will be imposed on you even if you're a scientist. He was attacked for two things. First, he said it's a \"reparative treatment\". They said, \"Why are you using the word \"reparative\"?\" That's the first thing they attacked him on. The second thing: he had to retract or apologize for his study, even though he didn't say in his apology, \"My study was wrong.\" He tried to justify what he did. Why? Because he was attacked, and you can see that if you research what happened to him. They brought him on Social Media, they attacked him, they pressed him on the research that he did. So, if you do not accept that research, how can you know then whether something is innate or not? If we cannot conduct studies and studies are flawed, then how can we know?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Lesbian Speaks The Truth About LGTBQ! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9px3rIVstxI", ((871, "14:31–14:49"), (924, "15:24–16:11"),))
// U ML385:192-287 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("I'm going to talk about scientific research on the idea of homosexuality that demonstrates that it's not an innate thing. You've not given any evidence that it is innate, but I will give you evidence that it is not innate, from scientific research, from people who are not Muslims.", "There's a very good book written by two scientists called \"My genes made me do it\". It's all scientific research disproving this idea that innately you're born as a homosexual, and it gives many reasons. For example, it looks at identical twins: people who are born with the exact same genetics and everything, in the same environment. One of them is homosexual and one is not. If it's an innate genetic thing or something within your genes, then both of the twins will be having it. Identical twins by definition are people who have the same exact genes; this is what identical twins are scientifically.", "For example, Robert Spitzer conducted a study. He brought 200 homosexuals, and all he did is he spoke to them. All of them became heterosexual.", "I'm not talking about conversion therapy. I made an argument about Robert Spitzer: people who willingly went and had this treatment from Robert Spitzer. He didn't force anyone to do anything. This was published in Nature Magazine; this was not something that was done under the roof! If he did evil things, he would be in prison. America is one of the biggest countries that promote the LGBTQ. He's very well known, he has written multiple works, and his research is on Nature Magazine. In fact, he called it \"the reparative treatment\", and the media attacked him for using the term \"reparative\" because they said: you insinuated that something needs to be repaired. So they attacked him just for using that different term, let alone forcing anyone to do anything! People came willingly. 200 people, they became heterosexual, which is absolute evidence that this is something not innate.", "Now, another thing: Nature Magazine conducted a study in 2019. It's called \"No Gay Gene\" study. It spent billions of dollars trying to find any gene that links homosexual behaviour to the individual. So far, I've provided you a book, two research studies on Nature Magazine that disprove the idea that you're saying, that people are born innate. This is what science says. It's not what I'm saying, it's what science says. If you have a problem, it's with science, not with me.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Gay Student Confronts Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XqXTdyMc3OU", ((549, "9:09–9:19"), (563, "9:23–10:01"), (614, "10:14–10:22"), (680, "11:20–12:06"), (732, "12:12–12:39"),))
// U ML130:140-227 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("My argument is: I don't need to prove that you're not born with a homosexual tendency. I don't need to do that. YOU make the claim. So you need to prove that. I'm showing you: here are contradictory studies.", "So you have this study, it says, \"No Gay Gene\". And it was the LGBT community: people from that community or people who support them who conducted the study, because they're trying to show evidence that: \"we want to prove genetically that this is a genetic thing\". They ended up themselves saying that there is no such thing! There's no gay gene, there's no proof that you have this sexual orientation due to genetic composition. That's their own claim, from the mouth of the horse.", "By the way, they edited it recently, but they still don't say there is any group of genes, whether one or more, that determines you being homosexual. Find me that in the study: where is that? I read this article. I download a page, because when you download the page, you have the original page before they edit it. I do that sometimes. I take screenshots and I download it, or I go to \"archive.org\". You can try to do that: go to \"archive.org\", and you will see how every little bit they keep editing this one, because this article was quoted so much by people who are from the opposite side. So now they started to make the wording as diplomatic as possible.", "But still, the study was conducted to show that there are genes, one or more, that make a human being with a homosexual tendency. But there isn't! And it's admitting that there isn't. All it's saying is: \"Yes, there are genes that can contribute to this\". All this is a whole bunch of nothing. We already knew all of that. We're talking about now the genes that are specific to the idea of being homosexual. There's no such thing: neither a combination of genes, nor one gene.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tran$gender Challenges Muslim On His Comments About LGTBQ Community! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XPGGQKYFYqo", ((419, "6:59–7:16"), (516, "8:36–9:04"), (575, "9:35–10:15"), (624, "10:24–10:50"),))
// U ML385:149-189 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("For us as Muslims, we're not hard materialists. So we don't believe that everything that happens metaphysically is just what happens in your body. So for example, we say that love is a metaphysical concept. It's not something you can put under a microscope and measure; love and hate and all of these things. They're all metaphysical, but we say there are chemicals that happen when you feel the feeling of love. But you're making a problem here; you're saying: just because there's a correlation, they both happen in the same time, there's a causation. Correlation does not entail causation. For example, if I drink water every time you go into the shop, does that mean me drinking water takes you to go inside the shop? So there is a link here that you're missing.", "I'm not denying that there are chemicals that happen when you have these feelings. I'm saying you cannot prove that because there's a chemical happening when the feeling is happening, it is happening because of the chemical!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Gay Student Confronts Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XqXTdyMc3OU", ((426, "7:06–7:39"), (496, "8:16–8:21"),))
