#passage(("Robert Spitzer conducted a study with 200 homosexuals. He spoke to them on the phone. He asked them questions. He realised many of them had issues when they were younger: some sort of treatment with the parents, abuse, stuff like that. He talked to them. And he's a psychologist. I'm not a psychologist, so I can't tell you exactly what he did. But he did a method of psychology with them. He spoke with them. And if something is innate in that way, it cannot change by anyone talking to you.", "That study was in Nature Magazine until that time. And you can trace it. You'll find it in archive.org, for example, how it was there. And you'll find it in other websites. Anyone can just Google \"Robert Spitzer Homosexual Study\" or \"Reparative Study\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Grills Muslim With Difficult And Inquisitive Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eOPafAukvyc", ((477, "7:57–8:40"), (570, "9:30–9:43"),))
// U ML238:203-270 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The individuals that would feel a part of the LGBTQ: most of them, I don't want to say all of them, have had some sort of a negative experience with a family member. It's fair for someone who is external of that group to say that there could be a link, a correlation, related to causation as well, between these two things happening.", "If you go back [50] years ago or 60 years ago, homosexuality or LGBTQ in general, it was very negative in society; it was taken as a negative thing, and that changed after sexual Revolution. But before the sexual Revolution, if you look at the medical text books, what was the medical position towards homosexuality or LGBTQ? They labeled it as a mental disease. In the medical textbooks they did not link it to parents; they linked it to external abuse: abuse from someone when you were young, when you're child. Especially when it came to men being gay, they would link it up to someone being sodomized as a child. The reason it changed was not science. The position of the society about LGBTQ or that group did not change because of science; more of public pressure and social pressure and sexual Revolution is the reason.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Transgender Confronts Muslim On LGTBQ! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eGnyoF1UOh0", ((487, "8:07–8:50"), (539, "8:59–10:11"),))
