#passage(("Generally, this is what I was trying to say: I take general scientific research, and based on that general scientific research, I draw the conclusion whether something is innate or not, depending on the research and what the research says. If someone wants to convince me, he needs to show me good enough evidence, and that doesn't mean I'm denying this or accepting that. I'm just saying, in general, if you want to convince me of that idea, you have to present me evidence. But if you tell me anecdotal evidence, for example, I say to you, \"I was born this way, I feel this way. Therefore, it's true.\", I say that argument can be used by so many. You can say, \"I'm born this way, I feel this way, therefore, it's true.\" But that is not evidence. Evidence is: the majority of people are born with a specific tendency. Scientific research showed the opposite to the claim that this is an innate thing. That's what I can take.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Lesbian Speaks The Truth About LGTBQ! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9px3rIVstxI", ((1288, "21:28–22:11"),))

