#passage(("The reason you follow the Quran is because the Quran doesn't change. So what about the part of the Quran that tells you you are born a man or you're born a woman? You're born what you are; there's no such thing about feelings when it comes to the Quran.", "The number of people that changed your gender in the US in comparison to the rest of the world: there's no comparison of the amount, the huge massive number that do in the US in comparison to the rest of the world. I'm referring to today, in this day and age, in which, by law in the west, you're allowed to do this; in fact you're protected, like in the UK. Of course the liberalism has taken over the West in general, but I'm saying: if it's taken over the West, why does the US still have more numbers than the rest of the world? I would say it comes down to the culture and society as well, and what the community is telling you when you find the safe haven with the group of LGBTQ in your school: \"we are acceptance for every whatever it is\". And then you want to be a part of that. So you say, \"You know what, I'm actually feeling something else,\" or, \"Today I identify as whatever it is,\" in order for you to feel a part of that group or Community. That would make sense to the number of people doing it here in the US in comparison to the rest of the world.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Transgender Confronts Muslim On LGTBQ! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eGnyoF1UOh0", ((283, "4:43–4:52"), (345, "5:45–7:17"),))
