#passage(("Very simply, I would ask you, what is a man? When you said to me that a man is someone who identifies as a man, that's a circular definition. In essence, you're saying a man is a man.", "The Creator is Wise. I'm saying the person born without the arm: there is wisdom behind that, and what he does in the future is a different story. So, you were saying \"someone born in a specific way which is wrong\"; I'm saying the natural way that someone is born, we don't say that is wrong. There's a difference between what you will do in the future, which is having a prosthetic arm or whatever it is.", "I'm asking you, \"What is a man?\", because you said you were born as a man but in the wrong body. When you say, \"I'm born as a man,\" you should be able to tell me what a man is. I define a man as an adult male; that's my definition of a man. A man is an adult male, and to me a woman is an adult female that becomes pregnant and gives birth. That's my belief as a Muslim. That's what the Quran preaches. It's what Islam teaches.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Discussion With A Tunisian Transgender! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I3TbyQWi60k", ((312, "5:12–6:02"), (393, "6:33–7:05"), (471, "7:51–8:42"),))
